            <ArticleTitle>[Dorsopathy in the elderly: pathobiology and multimodality therapy in clinical practice].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The lecture considers the most common causes of dorsopathy in elderly patients, by taking into account pathobiology, age markers, and aging processes. It discusses the general issues in the management of elderly patients, including advice on exercise and treatment; particular emphasis is placed on vitamin B group-containing xefocam and neurobion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
